<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<project xmlns="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0"
         xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
         xsi:schemaLocation="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0 http://maven.apache.org/xsd/maven-4.0.0.xsd">
    <modelVersion>4.0.0</modelVersion>

    <parent>
        <groupId>org.iromu.embabel.smith</groupId>
        <artifactId>embabel-smith-poc</artifactId>
        <version>0.1.0-SNAPSHOT</version>
    </parent>

    <artifactId>poc-27-recursive-self-improvement</artifactId>
    <name>poc-27-recursive-self-improvement</name>
    <description>
        POC 27: asks how much of embabel-smith's improvement loop can be made self-referential — can
        the process that builds be improved, including the part that does the improving, without
        grading its own homework. The loop in the studio improves only the prompts of the steps that
        failed and cannot touch the generator that wrote them, and a builder-built pack is stamped
        with a baseline equal to its own build-time score, so the strict gate comparison can never
        pass. This POC fixes an interpreter (the Embabel platform, the scorer, the frozen task set,
        the labelled trace corpus) and mutates only artifacts that interpreter runs: generated agent
        specs, generated JavaScript skill scripts run through POC 26's GraalJS engine, and a
        generated improvement policy expressed as one of those scripts. Improvement is measured as a
        derivative across at least two generations against a noise floor recorded before any tuning,
        and every variant is kept in an archive rather than hill-climbed.
    </description>

    <dependencies>
        <!-- The in-JVM SkillScriptExecutionEngine the generated policies and skill scripts run on.
             It reaches the ACTOR side of this module only; the referee (task 3.2) never constructs
             one, and poc-26's dependency here is why isolation is by process boundary rather than
             by absent jars. -->
        <dependency>
            <groupId>org.iromu.embabel.smith</groupId>
            <artifactId>poc-26-graaljs-skill-scripts</artifactId>
        </dependency>

        <!-- The product's gate, reused exactly as it is: GateChain's two-argument constructor takes
             the frozen task list and an invoker factory, which is the only seam the referee needs
             (design D2, docs/10-self-improvement.md:8-12). prod/ is not modified.

             The improvement engine itself is builder logic (change: builder-owns-improvement-loop), so
             nothing here compiles against the studio. It remains at test scope for one reason:
             LoopNeverPushesTest reads StudioConfiguration.class off the classpath to prove the push flag
             defaults to off, and that default lives in the studio's @Value, not in the builder's
             LoopPublishPolicy. Test scope keeps it off this POC's runtime classpath, so the launcher
             stays a plain application rather than a web one. The exclusions still apply, keeping the
             studio's web and database surface off even the test classpath: GateChain needs only
             smith-common and the builder, and spring-boot-starter-web, the JPA starter, the Postgres
             driver and spring-boot-docker-compose would otherwise pull Hibernate and compose
             auto-configuration in for a gate that uses none of it. -->
        <dependency>
            <groupId>org.iromu.embabel.smith</groupId>
            <artifactId>embabel-smith-studio</artifactId>
            <scope>test</scope>
            <exclusions>
                <exclusion>
                    <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>
                    <artifactId>spring-boot-starter-web</artifactId>
                </exclusion>
                <exclusion>
                    <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>
                    <artifactId>spring-boot-starter-data-jpa</artifactId>
                </exclusion>
                <exclusion>
                    <groupId>org.postgresql</groupId>
                    <artifactId>postgresql</artifactId>
                </exclusion>
                <exclusion>
                    <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>
                    <artifactId>spring-boot-docker-compose</artifactId>
                </exclusion>
            </exclusions>
        </dependency>
        <!-- EvalTask and InvokerFactory, the two types the gate is constructed over. -->
        <dependency>
            <groupId>org.iromu.embabel.smith</groupId>
            <artifactId>embabel-smith-builder</artifactId>
        </dependency>
        <!-- AgentSpec, the candidate the gate judges. -->
        <dependency>
            <groupId>org.iromu.embabel.smith</groupId>
            <artifactId>smith-common</artifactId>
        </dependency>
        <!-- The frozen task JSON is read here rather than through the product's codecs, which do not
             know this format. -->
        <dependency>
            <groupId>com.fasterxml.jackson.core</groupId>
            <artifactId>jackson-databind</artifactId>
        </dependency>

        <dependency>
            <groupId>org.junit.jupiter</groupId>
            <artifactId>junit-jupiter</artifactId>
            <scope>test</scope>
        </dependency>
        <dependency>
            <groupId>org.assertj</groupId>
            <artifactId>assertj-core</artifactId>
            <scope>test</scope>
        </dependency>
    </dependencies>

    <build>
        <plugins>
            <plugin>
                <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>
                <artifactId>spring-boot-maven-plugin</artifactId>
            </plugin>
        </plugins>
    </build>
</project>
